  "metric": "FP32 dense vector peak",
  "unit": "TFLOPS",
  "definition": "One TFLOPS is 10^12 32-bit floating-point arithmetic operations per second. This dataset uses standard CUDA/vector arithmetic, excluding TF32, FP16/BF16, tensor/matrix substitutes and sparse multipliers.",
  "aggregation": "Sum of per-device theoretical capacity for a known positive integer count of identical full GPUs. This is aggregate installed arithmetic capacity, not a claim of linear application or Geekbench scaling.",
  "sourcePolicy": "Prefer a provider-specific published FP32 figure. Otherwise join an exact provider hardware model/variant to a primary manufacturer peak specification and explicitly label it as a hardware-model proxy.",
  "limitations": [
    "Theoretical peak is not measured VM or application performance. Cloud clocks and power limits may differ from the manufacturer peak.",
    "Fractional, virtualized, unknown, heterogeneous, or conflicting accelerator mappings are excluded. A known integer GPU count is required.",
    "GPU model specifications are reviewed separately from daily prices; their retrievedAt date is not advanced by a price refresh.",
    "FP32 throughput is a GPU predictor. It is not imputed for CPUs from vCPU counts.",
    "Multiple VM configurations using the same GPU model do not represent independent performance measurements."
  ],
